    "title": "A=1 quadratic minimum-pair oriented-gcd coupling",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "forward/reverse split pencils force a linear center-owned gcd",
    "statement": "At pair union rho+3, source exclusion sharpens an oriented rank-two common-gcd degree to g>=max(1,ceil((r_sigma e-2)/(r_sigma+2))). If both endpoint deficits vanish, the forward and reverse gcd root sets exchange the endpoints and share their other g-1 roots; all six residual row-root sets are pairwise disjoint, forcing 5g>=3e-2. Hence every minimum pair has an oriented center-owned common divisor of degree at least ceil((3e-2)/5), ceil((e-2)/3), or ceil((e-1)/2) according as the maximum endpoint deficit is 0, 1, or 2.",
